description:
Lists the page the reader reached on each day of one reading of a book in their ReadingRate library: for each day, the furthest page, the page they left off at, the pages read and the percent of their copy.

Use when the user asks how far they got each day, how many pages they read on which days, how long a book took them day by day, or wants a chart of their progress through a book. For the books themselves, their status and dates, use get_reading_history.

ReadingRate records each change of page from the time this history began, so days before logged_since are unknown, not unread. Days are counted in timezone: give the reader's IANA time zone when known (for example "Europe/London"); otherwise their notification setting is used, else UTC.

Examples:
- {"book_id": "<book id>"}
- {"book_id": "<book id>", "timezone": "Europe/London"}
- {"book_id": "<book id>", "reading_number": 1}
